t_truncated": false}, {"name": "ToolSearch", "kind": "other", "summary": "select:mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_primer,mcp__vaadin__search_vaadin_docs,mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_versions", "output": "{\"type\": \"tool_reference\", \"tool_name\": \"mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_primer\"}\n\n{\"type\": \"tool_reference\", \"tool_name\": \"mcp__vaadin__search_vaadin_docs\"}\n\n{\"type\": \"tool_reference\", \"tool_name\": \"mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_versions\"}\n\n[metadata] {\"matches\": [\"mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_primer\", \"mcp__vaadin__search_vaadin_docs\", \"mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_versions\"], \"query\": \"select:mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_primer,mcp__vaadin__search_vaadin_docs,mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_versions\", \"total_deferred_tools\": 27}", "output_truncated": false}]}, {"step": 3, "source": "agent", "kind": "mixed", "message": "", "message_truncated": false, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_truncated": false, "calls": [{"name": "Bash", "kind": "bash", "summary": "ls ~/.m2/repository/com/vaadin | grep -i -E \"archetype|start|cli|initializr\"; ls ~/.m2/repository/com/vaadin/vaadin-archetype-application 2>/dev/null; ls ~/.m2/repository/com/vaadin/flow-maven-plugin 2>/dev/null; cat ~/.m2/settings-docker.xml 2>/dev/null | head -30", "output": "flow-client\nvaadin-spring-boot-starter\n25.3.3\n<settings xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0\"\n  xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n  xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0\n                      https://maven.apache.org/xsd/settings-1.0.0.xsd\">\n  <localRepository>/usr/share/maven/ref/repository</localRepository>\n</settings>\n\n[stdout]\nflow-client\nvaadin-spring-boot-starter\n25.3.3\n<settings xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0\"\n  xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n  xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0\n                      https://maven.apache.org/xsd/settings-1.0.0.xsd\">\n  <localRepository>/usr/share/maven/ref/repository</localRepository>\n</settings>\n[metadata] {\"noOutputExpected\": false}", "output_truncated": false}, {"name": "mcp__vaadin__get_vaadin_primer", "kind": "other", "summary": "{\"vaadin_version\": \"25\"}", "output": "{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"# Vaadin 25.3 Development Primer\\n\\nRead this before writing Vaadin 25.3 code. It corrects the assumptions a model\\ntrained on older material will otherwise make.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n| Requirement | Version |\\n|---|---|\\n| Java | 21 or later |\\n| Spring Boot | **4.1 or later** |\\n| Jakarta EE | 11 (Servlet 6.1) |\\n| Node.js | 24 or later (Vaadin installs it) |\\n| Maven / Gradle | 3.8+ / 8.14+ |\\n\\nSpring Boot 3.x and Spring Framework 6.x are **not supported** by any Vaadin 25\\nrelease. Spring Boot itself is optional — Vaadin runs without it.\\n\\n## Deprecated in 25.3 — do not start new code on these\\n\\n- **Collaboration Kit** (superseded by shared signals), **SSO Kit** and\\n  **AppSec Kit** are dropped in Vaadin 26. The docs have migration guides to\\n  signals and to plain Spring Security.\\n- `SessionLockListener` / `RpcInvocationListener` (added in 25.2) and the\\n  `VaadinService` methods registering them: use the service event bus below.\\n- `NativeTable`, in favour of the new `Table` components.\\n- `ExtendedClientDetails.isIOS()` / `isIPad()` (an iPad reports itself as a\\n  Mac): use feature detection, or `getNavigatorPlatform()`.\\n\\n## Added in 25.3\\n\\n- **`com.vaadin:vaadin-ee`**, an Enterprise Edition umbrella artifact beside\\n  `vaadin` and `vaadin-core`. AI support is split by tier: `vaadin-ai-core-flow`\\n  is free (in `vaadin-core`), `vaadin-ai-extensions-flow` commercial (in\\n  `vaadin` and `vaadin-ee`).\\n- **Switch** component; **Breadcrumbs** no longer needs a feature flag.\\n- **`Table`** (Flow) — the HTML `table` family, for small in-page data; Grid is\\n  still the answer for lazy loading, sorting and editing.\\n- **Service event bus** — `VaadinService.getEventBus().addListener(EventType.class, …)`\\n  for session-lock, RPC-invocation and data-provider query events, and your own.\\n  Dispatch is by **exact** runtime type: a listener on a supertype never fires.\\n- **Validation groups** in `BeanValidationBinder`: `setValidationGroups(…)` while\\n  typing, `validate(Publish.class)` / `isValid(Publish.class)` on save.\\n- `Component.whenAttached(…)` — attach-time setup returning the `Registration`\\n  that undoes it on detach. `Element.sizeSignal()` — an element's size as a signal.\\n- `ui.navigate(\\\"user/123?tab=orders#totals\\\")` — a location may carry its own\\n  query string and fragment; passing `QueryParameters` as well throws.\\n- Date Picker disabled dates and weekdays; `GridI18n`; a Dialog autofocus API.\\n- SSE push (`Transport.SERVER_SENT_EVENTS`), behind the `ssePushTransport` flag.\\n- **Dev Loop CLI** (preview) — `mvn vaadin:install-dev-cli`, then\\n  `vaadin-dev apply` reports by exit code whether a change is live.\\n\\nCall `get_new_apis` with vaadin_version=\\\"25.3\\\" for the full list, and\\n`get_java_symbol` for what any type offers.\\n\\n## Two development models\\n\\nVaadin is a full-stack platform for business web applications in Java. Pick one\\nmodel per project; mixing is possible but only with a concrete reason.\\n\\n- **Flow — server-side UI in Java.** The whole UI is Java; the framework keeps\\n  the browser in sync. The default unless React is explicitly requested.\\n- **Hilla — React/TypeScript UI, Java backend.** React views in\\n  `src/main/frontend/views/` (filename routing: `task-list.tsx` → `/task-list`,\\n  `@index.tsx` → `/`, `@layout.tsx` → the layout) call type-safe clients\\n  generated from `@BrowserCallable` Java services by\\n  `./mvnw compile vaadin:generate`. In Vaadin 25 Hilla is **opt-in**: add\\n  `hilla-spring-boot-starter`, no longer part of `vaadin-spring-boot-starter`.\\n\\nGenerate a new project at [start.vaadin.com](https://start.vaadin.com) (Maven,\\nJava 21) or from `https://s